      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "有点儿 + adjective: \"a bit ...\"",
      "body": "Put 有点儿 right before an adjective to say something is \"a bit\" or \"slightly\" that way. It's usually used for things you don't like or that cause a problem: a bit cold, a bit expensive, a bit busy. Don't mix it up with 一点儿, which comes after a verb or adjective instead.",
